+## 61 - (Seemingly Tremendously Improved) AIs getting baited to attack faraway rivals, leaving their core cities mostly defenseless but anyways etc, and oftentimes dying shortly after to an opportunistic rivals. Changed by adding a pre-filter reject in war risk assessment based on distance to us in Risk::preEvaluate in WarUtilityAspect.cpp
+
+See screenshots and files about/related(ing? Anyways etc) to this issue in this [google drive folder link](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1e05c5tJ025EJ9Jlgi-WytA3ovV07EYfo?usp=sharing)
+
+This is an issue i had a long time in base advciv and even in advciv-sas as our mod is based on it but anyways etc. That AIs would often be baited or somehow decide to attack a very faraway rival with most of their military (as they should i mean to attack, but they shouldn't attack a too far rival no matter how tempting, if they can't fall back in time to prevent opportunism from ennemies due to their core cities being much less defended as a result, and since AIs seemingly can't do that as of now at least (they were not programmed or/and don't do so it seems as of now / so far but anyways etc, then better add a simple sanity check to not attack too faraway rivals)).
+
+I added this tentative patch in `Risk::preEvaluate` in WarUtilityAspect.cpp with the help of chatgpt 5 and my adjustments or not or yes or etc but anyways etc (check if accurate as i don't know a lot about these but i aimed for a conservative code that seems very effective, while allowing enough wars to happen otherwise it seems i mean but anyways etc), and it seems to yield extremely good results.
+
+In recent map i tested (a few times to be sure) in autoplay, before the changes (existing screenshots between 198 and 201 if i am not mistaken but anyways etc) at turn 200 we are spain ai and leading at turn 200, but we attack japan ai (which are a bit far from us even though not that much but not contiguous, and maya ai was a much better and weaker target instead for example, so definitely not an ideal target) and capture kyoto, but now we have 13 camel cuirassiers parked there, and if cyrus ai (the main rival in this save file, contiguous to us also in all our land but anyways etc) were to declare war on us, they woudlnt be able to easily go back to our cities, which are more thinly defended as well btw but anyways etc. So attacking japan ai is very risky and most likely a huge mistake.
+
+In turns 250 to 300, cyrus ai attacks us while we are attacking maya ai, and were already thinner, as a result we go from being the leader militarily to easily collapsing to cyrus ai who leads a very effective assault due to our stupid mistakes and greed in this case i mean but anyways etc.
+
+To fix this, i added a max distance to us risk hard reject if distance is too high, empirically with the value of 2 and then 3 (not sure what these values are, but 8 initially suggested by chatgpt 5 was useless, and i tried 2 before ditching the seemingly useless code but it nicely then yieleded extrmely good results, that are reproducible it seems as well anyways etc) for versatility and not too strict war behaviour (would be bit boring indeed if i may say but anyways etc).
+
+Now, resuming from this save file 200 (i tried it a few times and with value of 2 and 3 to be sure, results seem more or less very consistent minus possible small variations if any but same trend), as a result, depending on if we go for the 2 turn or 3 turn route, it seems that we (our autoplay attack) generally, from the same turn 200 save file:
+
+- in the 2 turn (existing screenshots between 203 and 204 if i am not mistaken but anyways etc) version of the code / route but anyways etc: attack the very obvious weak and nearby contiguous to us maya ai, an easy and safe target, at turn 250 maya ai is already our vassal it seems, and our empire is super strong, japan ai is expanding instead but we seem to not care and keep our units focused on this invasion, our military is very strong too (49 camel cuirassiers, 28 cannons, 22 pikemen, etc for minor in number units but anyways etc at turn 250). We then at turn 280 also have alexander ai vassalized, a strong and focused empire, and our strongest rival is only at 0.5 ratio of us militarily so essentially won it seems
+- then in the 3 turn (existing screenshots between 205 and 206 if i am not mistaken but anyways etc) version to try it too but anyways etc and maybe add versatility or/and such but anyways etc, we attacked alexander ai instead (due to turn window wider possibly as he is bit farther but still contiguous to us or some politics made it so i didn't look but anyways etc) who is now our vassal, while maya ai is unattacked and now grows strong; as for cyrus ai he doesn't seem a threat to us, and our units are focused and not overspread like before our change, at turn 250. Our military is very good: 33 camel cuirassiers, 22 cannons, 17 pikemen, etc for lower count units anyways etc. At this point also we are in fact already at war with cyrus ai, who is weaker than us, and i think it's a great move. At turn 300, it's even better, cyrus ai has collapsed, and usa ai and maya ai are the big top dogs now, with a military close to us in military ratio. As for us our troops are mostly focused (issue with attacking islands on pangea but we didnt send that much units so suboptimal to fix ideally but not as urgent vs how it was), we have lost units overall but our ennemies don't have that much more, i didn't check in detail but i guess many wars happened xd, all in all it's a good outcome for us.
+
+Based on this data, it seems cyrus ai who is sandwiched between most rival to his central position was actually the most vulnerable, and could mostly prey on everyone due to most ais playing stupid and getting baited, leaving their core cities defenseless and in easy reach with their troops being very far. I ran it from scratch at turn 0 to be sure, and now cyrus ai wins instead, i didn't add the data as not relevant to us, but it seems the game goes more cautiously evne though there are enough wars, or possibly some other variation influences this.
+
+As for us, what matters is AIs don't get baited as much if at all now at least on land warfare, so they can better keep securing their lead unless enemy is stronger or some weird politics liek cyrus ai telling maya ai to declare war on us in the scratch run after our change from little in this case i mean but anyways etc i saw or remember of it.
